SUMMARY:Panigiri of Koumoulo\, Menites
LOCATION:Menites\, Andros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Menites\, the village of running water and plane trees above Chora\, holds its Koumoulo panigiri on 23 August from 21:00 in the square\, run by the cultural association with free entry: local food\, wine and live island music. Katakoilos has its own big square panigiri on a nearby night (22-24 August)\, so you can do both in a weekend.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#menites-panigiri-of-koumoulo-menites
